FILE Program.cs

TYPE Book           : record with Id (int), Title (string), Year (int, optional)
TYPE NewBook        : record with Title, Year
TYPE LibraryOptions : class with Name, Greeting (strings, with defaults)
TYPE RequestStamp   : class with a short random Id, set once when created
TYPE ShelfStore     : class holding a list of Book (start with two), a lock, and the next Id
                      All(), Find(id), Add(NewBook) -> Book

---- 1. BUILDER ----
CREATE builder
REGISTER services
  ShelfStore      as SINGLETON   (one for the whole app)
  RequestStamp    as SCOPED      (one per request)
  Problem Details                (standard JSON error bodies)
BIND configuration section "Library" to LibraryOptions

---- 2. APP ----
BUILD app

---- 3. MIDDLEWARE (in this order) ----
USE exception handler         (unhandled exception -> 500 Problem Details)
USE status code pages         (empty 404/405 -> Problem Details body)
USE inline middleware
  START a stopwatch
  BEFORE the response starts: SET header X-Elapsed-Ms
  CALL next
  LOG method, path, status, elapsed

---- 4. ENDPOINTS ----
GET /                -> read "Library:Greeting" from IConfiguration, return it as text
GET /hello/{name}    -> "Hello, {name}!"; IF query shout=true, upper-case it
GET /whoami          -> JSON: library name (from options), request stamp Id, User-Agent header

GROUP /shelf
  GET /              -> query max (int, default 50); return up to max books
  GET /{id:int}      -> 200 with the book, or 404
  POST /             -> read NewBook from the JSON body
                        IF title blank: RETURN 400 validation problem for "title"
                        ADD, RETURN 201 with Location "/shelf/{id}"

GET /boom            -> THROW an exception (to see the exception handler work)

IF environment is Development
  GET /debug/env     -> JSON: environment name, application name, content root

---- 5. RUN ----
RUN app

NOTE
  Handlers get their inputs from parameters. ASP.NET Core decides where each comes from:
    name in the route template       -> route
    registered service type          -> container
    simple type, not in the route    -> query string
    complex type (record/class)      -> JSON body
    [FromHeader]                     -> header
